V3DRender 0.08: kit 9, Z store or tile-buffer reads?
=====================================================

Kit 8: turning the V3D's power domain off and on through the firmware
changed nothing; Mesa's Z store still never finishes, wherever it
writes.

Mesa's depth buffer is Z24S8 (depth and stencil in one word), and its
job stores only Z into it. To keep the stencil bits, the GPU may have
to read the buffer's memory back while it stores. V3DJob's own tests
have never made the tile buffer read memory. Replay now also runs the
job:

  - storing Z+stencil (11) instead of Z (9);
  - storing stencil (10) instead of Z;
  - loading colour into the tile from memory first (no Z store);
  - loading Z+stencil into the tile from memory first (no Z store).

If the loads hang too, the GPU's tile buffer can't read memory here;
if Z+stencil stores work, it's the partial (read-back) store.

Before you start
- A Pi 4, Pi 400 or CM4 with RISC OS 5.30 or later. V3DDriver not
  loaded. Copy this folder to a hard disc.

The test
1. Double-click Replay. It loads V3DRender 0.08 from this folder, in
   place of an older one. No program should be using the GPU at the same time:
   Replay needs the buffer addresses Mesa's job had.
2. Optional: double-click Check too (kits 1-5's tests, all passed in
   kit 5).
3. Send Results back.
